15:06:37 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Victoria and Albert Museum\n1. The Victoria and Albert Museum houses a diverse and varied collection of art, artifacts, and photographs.', 'Victoria and Albert Museum\n2. Some collections within the museum are unique and unconventional, such as the Eadweard Muybridge photographs of Animal Locomotion.', "Victoria and Albert Museum\n3. The museum's collection spans over different time periods, ranging from the late 19th century to the early 20th century.", 'Victoria and Albert Museum\n4. The museum has a collection of society portraits by James Lafayette, showcasing prominent figures from the period.', "Victoria and Albert Museum\n5. The museum's collection includes photographs of notable individuals from various fields, such as bishops, generals, and entertainers.", "Victoria and Albert Museum\n6. The collection features photographs of events and occasions, such as the ball held at Devonshire House in 1897 to celebrate Queen Victoria's diamond jubilee.", 'Victoria and Albert Museum\n7. The Eadweard Muybridge photographs provide a unique visual representation of animal movements in a fraction of a second.', "Victoria and Albert Museum\n8. The museum's collection covers different genres, including society portraits, street life in London, and animal locomotion.", 'Victoria and Albert Museum\n9. The James Lafayette society portraits offer a glimpse into the social and cultural life of the period.', "Victoria and Albert Museum\n10. The museum's collection showcases the intersection of art, photography, and history.", "Victoria and Albert Museum\nOne of the more unusual collections is that of Eadweard Muybridge's photographs of Animal Locomotion of 1887, this consists of 781 plates. These sequences of photographs taken a fraction of a second apart capture images of different animals and humans performimg various actions. There are several of John Thomson's 1876-7 images of Street Life in London in the collection. The museum also holds James Lafayette's society portraits, a collection of more than 600 photographs dating from the late 19th to early 20th centuries and portraying a wide range of society figures of the period, including bishops, generals, society ladies, Indian maharajas, Ethiopian rulers and other foreign leaders, actresses, people posing in their motor cars and a sequence of photographs recording the guests at the famous fancy-dress ball held at Devonshire House in 1897 to celebrate Queen Victoria's diamond jubilee."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': "One of the more unusual collections is that of Eadweard Muybridge's photographs of Animal Locomotion of 1887, this consists of 781 plates. These sequences of photographs taken a fraction of a second apart capture images of different animals and humans performimg various actions. There are several of John Thomson's 1876-7 images of Street Life in London in the collection. The museum also holds James Lafayette's society portraits, a collection of more than 600 photographs dating from the late 19th to early 20th centuries and portraying a wide range of society figures of the period, including bishops, generals, society ladies, Indian maharajas, Ethiopian rulers and other foreign leaders, actresses, people posing in their motor cars and a sequence of photographs recording the guests at the famous fancy-dress ball held at Devonshire House in 1897 to celebrate Queen Victoria's diamond jubilee.", 'question': 'Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nWho created the photographic series titled Animal Locomotion?', 'answer': 'Eadweard Muybridge'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': "One of the more unusual collections is that of Eadweard Muybridge's photographs of Animal Locomotion of 1887, this consists of 781 plates. These sequences of photographs taken a fraction of a second apart capture images of different animals and humans performimg various actions. There are several of John Thomson's 1876-7 images of Street Life in London in the collection. The museum also holds James Lafayette's society portraits, a collection of more than 600 photographs dating from the late 19th to early 20th centuries and portraying a wide range of society figures of the period, including bishops, generals, society ladies, Indian maharajas, Ethiopian rulers and other foreign leaders, actresses, people posing in their motor cars and a sequence of photographs recording the guests at the famous fancy-dress ball held at Devonshire House in 1897 to celebrate Queen Victoria's diamond jubilee.", 'question': 'Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nIn which year was the Animal Locomotion collection created?', 'answer': '1887'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': "One of the more unusual collections is that of Eadweard Muybridge's photographs of Animal Locomotion of 1887, this consists of 781 plates. These sequences of photographs taken a fraction of a second apart capture images of different animals and humans performimg various actions. There are several of John Thomson's 1876-7 images of Street Life in London in the collection. The museum also holds James Lafayette's society portraits, a collection of more than 600 photographs dating from the late 19th to early 20th centuries and portraying a wide range of society figures of the period, including bishops, generals, society ladies, Indian maharajas, Ethiopian rulers and other foreign leaders, actresses, people posing in their motor cars and a sequence of photographs recording the guests at the famous fancy-dress ball held at Devonshire House in 1897 to celebrate Queen Victoria's diamond jubilee.", 'question': 'Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nHow many photographic plates comprise the Animal Locomotion collection?', 'answer': '781'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': "One of the more unusual collections is that of Eadweard Muybridge's photographs of Animal Locomotion of 1887, this consists of 781 plates. These sequences of photographs taken a fraction of a second apart capture images of different animals and humans performimg various actions. There are several of John Thomson's 1876-7 images of Street Life in London in the collection. The museum also holds James Lafayette's society portraits, a collection of more than 600 photographs dating from the late 19th to early 20th centuries and portraying a wide range of society figures of the period, including bishops, generals, society ladies, Indian maharajas, Ethiopian rulers and other foreign leaders, actresses, people posing in their motor cars and a sequence of photographs recording the guests at the famous fancy-dress ball held at Devonshire House in 1897 to celebrate Queen Victoria's diamond jubilee.", 'question': 'Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nWhat do the Animal Locomotion photographs capture?', 'answer': 'animals and humans performimg various actions'}, {'title': 'Victoria and Albert Museum', 'context': "One of the more unusual collections is that of Eadweard Muybridge's photographs of Animal Locomotion of 1887, this consists of 781 plates. These sequences of photographs taken a fraction of a second apart capture images of different animals and humans performimg various actions. There are several of John Thomson's 1876-7 images of Street Life in London in the collection. The museum also holds James Lafayette's society portraits, a collection of more than 600 photographs dating from the late 19th to early 20th centuries and portraying a wide range of society figures of the period, including bishops, generals, society ladies, Indian maharajas, Ethiopian rulers and other foreign leaders, actresses, people posing in their motor cars and a sequence of photographs recording the guests at the famous fancy-dress ball held at Devonshire House in 1897 to celebrate Queen Victoria's diamond jubilee.", 'question': 'Topic: Victoria and Albert Museum\nWhose society portraits from the late 19th to ear