15:07:12 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Fresno, California\n1. Fresno, California went through a significant decline in the late 1960s and 1970s, which has now been overcome.', 'Fresno, California\n2. The revival of Fresno, California was initiated after the re-opening of the Tower Theatre in the late 1970s.', 'Fresno, California\n3. The Tower Theatre initially showed second and third run movies, along with classic films.', "Fresno, California\n4. Roger Rocka's Dinner Theater & Good Company Players opened near the Tower Theatre in 1978.", 'Fresno, California\n5. Fresno native Audra McDonald performed in the leading roles of Evita and The Wiz at the theater as a high school student.', 'Fresno, California\n6. Audra McDonald subsequently became a prominent performer on Broadway in New York City and won a Tony Award.', "Fresno, California\n7. The Tower Theatre still exists in the Tower District of Fresno, along with Good Company Players' 2nd Space Theatre.", "Fresno, California\nThis vibrant and culturally diverse area of retail businesses and residences experienced a renewal after a significant decline in the late 1960s and 1970s.[citation needed] After decades of neglect and suburban flight, the neighborhood revival followed the re-opening of the Tower Theatre in the late 1970s, which at that time showed second and third run movies, along with classic films. Roger Rocka's Dinner Theater & Good Company Players also opened nearby in 1978,[citation needed] at Olive and Wishon Avenues. Fresno native Audra McDonald performed in the leading roles of Evita and The Wiz at the theater while she was a high school student. McDonald subsequently became a leading performer on Broadway in New York City and a Tony award winning actress. Also in the Tower District is Good Company Players' 2nd Space Theatre."], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Fresno, California', 'context': "This vibrant and culturally diverse area of retail businesses and residences experienced a