15:23:33 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['Immune system\n1. During wake periods, the immune system is predominantly focused on maintaining a state of rest and preserving energy for optimal functionality during active times.', 'Immune system\n2. Effector cells such as cytotoxic natural killer cells and cytotoxic T lymphocytes are upregulated during wake periods to effectively combat invading pathogens.', 'Immune system\n3. Anti-inflammatory molecules like cortisol and catecholamines also peak during awake active times to regulate and maintain an appropriate immune response.', 'Immune system\n4. The activation of the pro-inflammatory state is more likely to occur during sleep times, when the body is at rest and less cognitively and physically impeded.', 'Immune system\n5. The presence of melatonin during sleep times may contribute to the activation of the pro-inflammatory state by counteracting the potentially damaging effects of free radicals produced during this period.', 'Immune system\nIn contrast, during wake periods differentiated effector cells, such as cytotoxic natural killer cells and CTLs (cytotoxic T lymphocytes), peak in order to elicit an effective response against any intruding pathogens. As well during awake active times, anti-inflammatory molecules, such as cortisol and catecholamines, peak. There are two theories as to why the pro-inflammatory state is reserved for sleep time. First, inflammation would cause serious cognitive and physical impairments if it were to occur during wake times. Second, inflammation may occur during sleep times due to the presence of melatonin. Inflammation causes a great deal of oxidative stress and the presence of melatonin during sleep times could actively counteract free radical production during this time.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'Immune system', 'context': 'In contrast, during wake periods differentiated effector cells, such as cytotoxic natural killer cells and CTLs (cytotoxic T lymphocytes), peak in order to elicit an effective response against any intruding pathogens. As well during awake active times, anti-inflammatory molecules, such as cortisol and catecholamines, peak. There are two theories as to why the pro-inflammatory state is reserved for sleep time. First, inflammation would cause serious cognitive and physical impairments if it were to occur during wake times. Second, inflammation may occur during sleep times due to the presence of melatonin. Inflammation causes a great deal of oxidative stress and the presence of melatonin during sleep times could actively counteract free radical production during this time.', 'question': 'Topic: Immune system\nWhat are examples of differentiated effector cells that peak during wake periods?', 'answer': 'cytotoxic natural killer cells and CTLs (cytotoxic T lymphocytes)'}, {'title': 'Immune system', 'context': 'In contrast, during wake periods differentiated effector cells, such as cytotoxic natural killer cells and CTLs (cytotoxic T lymphocytes), peak in order to elicit an effective response against any intruding pathogens. As well during awake active times, anti-inflammatory molecules, such as cortisol and catecholamines, peak. There are two theories as to why the pro-inflammatory state is reserved for sleep time. First, inflammation would cause serious cognitive and physical impairments if it were to occur during wake times. Second, inflammation may occur during sleep times due to the presence of melatonin. Inflammation causes a great deal of oxidative stress and the presence of melatonin during sleep times could actively counteract free radical production during this time.', 'question': 'Topic: Immune system\nWhat are two anti-inflammatory molecules that peak during awake hours?', 'answer': 'cortisol and catecholamines'}, {'title': 'Immune system', 'context': 'In contrast, during wake periods differentiated effector cells, such as cytotoxic natural killer cells and CTLs (cytotoxic T lymphocytes), peak in order to elicit an effective response against any intruding pathogens. As well during awake active times, anti-inflammatory molecules, such as cortisol and catecholamines, peak. There are two theories as to why the pro-inflammatory state is reserved for sleep time. First, inflammation would cause serious cognitive and physical impairments if it were to occur during wake times. Second, inflammation may occur during sleep times due to the presence of melatonin. Inflammation causes a great deal of oxidative stress and the presence of melatonin during sleep times could actively counteract free radical production during this time.', 'question': 'Topic: Immune system\nInflammation occurs during sleep times because of the presence of what molecule?', 'answer': 'melatonin'}, {'title': 'Immune system', 'context': 'In contrast, during wake periods differentiated effector cells, such as cytotoxic natural killer cells and CTLs (cytotoxic T lymphocytes), peak in order to elicit an effective response against any intruding pathogens. As well during awake active times, anti-inflammatory molecules, such as cortisol and catecholamines, peak. There are two theories as to why the pro-inflammatory state is reserved for sleep time. First, inflammation would cause serious cognitive and physical impairments if it were to occur during wake times. Second, inflammation may occur during sleep times due to the presence of melatonin. Inflammation causes a great deal of oxidative stress and the presence of melatonin during sleep times could actively counteract free radical production during this time.', 'question': 'Topic: Immune system\nMelatonin during sleep can actively counteract the production of what?', 'answer': 'free radical production'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
