15:26:20 [INFO] root - Received request: {'train_sequences': ['American Broadcasting Company\n1. ABC Radio wanted to compete with progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations in the 1960s, prompting the development of a new programming concept.', "American Broadcasting Company\n2. LOVE Radio was launched on ABC's FM stations in 1968, featuring a limited music selection.", "American Broadcasting Company\n3. In 1970, it was decided that ABC FM's music policy should be reviewed to include more styles of music, acknowledging its limited selection.", 'American Broadcasting Company\n4. LOVE Radio was a special programming project launched by ABC Radio, spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago.', 'American Broadcasting Company\n5. This project was established with the intention of competing with other stations of the time, specifically those with progressive rock and DJ-helmed formats.', "American Broadcasting Company\n6. After its initial launch, ABC's FM stations began to retain more of their original programming, such as KXYZ's continued use of their content.", 'American Broadcasting Company\n7. The launch of LOVE Radio marked a new direction for ABC Radio, moving away from their traditional offerings and seeking to attract new listeners with a more diverse music selection.', 'American Broadcasting Company\nIn July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.'], 'eval_questions': [{'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': "Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nWho lead the 1968 special programming for ABC Radio's FM stations?", 'answer': 'Allen Shaw'}, {'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': 'Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nWho was the ABC Radio president in 1968?', 'answer': 'Harold L. Neal'}, {'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': 'Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nWhat was the name for the new radio concept designed by Allen Shaw?', 'answer': 'LOVE Radio'}, {'title': 'American Broadcasting Company', 'context': 'In July 1968, ABC Radio launched a special programming project for its FM stations, which was spearheaded by Allen Shaw, a former program manager at WCFL in Chicago who was approached by ABC Radio president Harold L. Neal to develop a format to compete with the new progressive rock and DJ-helmed stations. The new concept called "LOVE Radio", which featured a limited selection of music genres, was launched on ABC\'s seven owned-and-operated FM stations in late November 1968; the concept replaced nearly all of the programming provided by these stations; however, several affiliates (such as KXYZ) retained the majority of their content. In August 1970, Shaw announced that ABC FM\'s music choice policy should be reviewed to allow listeners access to many styles of music.', 'question': 'Topic: American Broadcasting Company\nHow many ABC music stations were owned-and-operated in 1968?', 'answer': 'seven'}], 'lora_rank': 32, 'lora_alpha': 64, 'lora_dropout': 0.0, 'finetune_epochs': 10, 'finetune_lr': 0.001, 'batch_size': 1, 'gradient_accumulation_steps': 1, 'end_mask_substring': ''}
